WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.603 --> 00:00:04.443
Welcome to Key Stakeholder Roles in EBP Implementation.

2
00:00:05.243 --> 00:00:19.483
In this overview, you will learn how behavioral health practitioners, counties, Centers of Excellence, and the Department of Health Care Services work together to support evidence-based practice implementation and service delivery.

3
00:00:20.499 --> 00:00:26.259
Evidence-based practice, or EBP, implementation involves four key stakeholder groups.

4
00:00:26.979 --> 00:00:33.619
Each group has distinct responsibilities for supporting implementation, meeting requirements, and delivering services.

5
00:00:35.945 --> 00:00:46.105
Behavioral health practitioners complete required training, meet applicable quality requirements, deliver EBPs, and report required data.

6
00:00:46.505 --> 00:00:58.585
Counties coordinate implementation, support practitioners, ensure practitioners meet requirements, and submit Medi-Cal claims and individual and service-level encounters to DHCS.

7
00:00:58.985 --> 00:01:06.265
Centers of Excellence develop implementation resources and provide training, technical assistance, and quality support.

8
00:01:06.745 --> 00:01:15.305
DHCS establishes requirements and operational guidance, reviews data, oversees compliance, and addresses policy and payment questions.

9
00:01:16.736 --> 00:01:19.976
Together, these four roles form a connected system.

10
00:01:20.696 --> 00:01:24.536
DHCS establishes requirements and provides oversight.

11
00:01:25.496 --> 00:01:31.176
Centers of Excellence, or COEs, provide training, technical assistance, and quality support.

12
00:01:31.736 --> 00:01:35.656
Counties ensure their practitioners meet applicable requirements.

13
00:01:36.136 --> 00:01:40.296
Practitioners complete the requirements and deliver EBPs.

14
00:01:41.704 --> 00:01:44.184
You have learned about the four stakeholder groups.

15
00:01:44.664 --> 00:01:55.384
Select Continue to see how DHCS, COEs, counties, and behavioral health practitioners work together to support EBP implementation.
